(5007844, 728655, 61961, '<td valign="top">Hilarious shooting story.  Sorry you were subjected to the ridicule of passers-by!<br/></td>', 'Hilarious shooting story.  Sorry you were subjected to the ridicule of passers-by!', '2008-10-14 12:15:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5008115, 728273, 52549, '<td valign="top">I think you should have scored better than you did because this is an excellent image but I feel, in the end, the soft focus let you down. Your model is beautiful and her face more in focus, especially her eyes, would have given the image a more dramatic look.</td>', 'I think you should have scored better than you did because this is an excellent image but I feel, in the end, the soft focus let you down. Your model is beautiful and her face more in focus, especially her eyes, would have given the image a more dramatic look.', '2008-10-14 15:23:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5008121, 728673, 30791, '<td valign="top">I did a shoot a few days ago similar to the lighting situation here. i got that dark line in a few of my shots as well. i think it helps your shot though, im a little suprised it didnt show up in the reflection on the water as much as it did on the model.<br/>nice finish</td>', 'I did a shoot a few days ago similar to the lighting situation here. i got that dark line in a few of my shots as well. i think it helps your shot though, im a little suprised it didnt show up in the reflection on the water as much as it did on the model.nice finish', '2008-10-14 15:26:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5008122, 728615, 50695, '<td valign="top">something almost pre-Raphaelite about that image in the mirror. good work. nice to see you kicking timfy''s butt again!</td>', 'something almost pre-Raphaelite about that image in the mirror. good work. nice to see you kicking timfy''s butt again!', '2008-10-14 15:29:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5008132, 727495, 44516, '<td valign="top">amazing shot<br/></td>', 'amazing shot', '2008-10-14 15:41:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(5008235, 728615, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by aimeethetoo:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> Is there a reason why you didn''t just use the timer? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Sheesh man...give me some credit!  I may be blonde but... : )  I have several reasons for using the plunger...not the least of which was to allow me to stay put rather than continuously resetting myself (under black fabric - getting my hands and mirror right - resticking my cheapo fingernails, etc.).  It''s not like a simple bubble shot or deer head!  ;) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL.</td>', 'Originally posted by aimeethetoo: Originally posted by yanko: Is there a reason why you didn''t just use the timer?  Sheesh man...give me some credit!  I may be blonde but... : )  I have several reasons for using the plunger...not the least of which was to allow me to stay put rather than continuously resetting myself (under black fabric - getting my hands and mirror right - resticking my cheapo fingernails, etc.).  It''s not like a simple bubble shot or deer head!  ;)   LOL.', '2008-10-14 17:36:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5008557, 728615, 55397, '<td valign="top">Fantastic!  You''re amazing!</td>', 'Fantastic!  You''re amazing!', '2008-10-14 23:19:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5008576, 727735, 55397, '<td valign="top">What talent!  Not only did you make the photo, but you made the model!  And they''re both beautiful.</td>', 'What talent!  Not only did you make the photo, but you made the model!  And they''re both beautiful.', '2008-10-14 23:30:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5009196, 727495, 30807, '<td valign="top">To me, this is a lovely example of B&amp;W, and the water power is tremendous - very well done, a deserved ribbon!!<br/> <br/>Comparing with the colour, the dress is so much better, more visible, a completely different mood, and the only possible thing which in my view could perhaps make a difference, would be to lighten the hair some, so that we could see a bit more texture. My apologies if you can, but my CRT monitor can''t show me any. The water looks so powerful, as it has texture - I think a longer exposure would show it more as smoke, which would destroy the power - most effective just as is. <br/> <br/>I must admit that if I were going for a shot of the scene with no figure, I would love the colour shot, as they are lovely subtle colours - I don''t seem to be able to capture such myself, though I live just on the coast - sigh!<br/> <br/>Well done - will keep an eye for your future pix</td>', 'To me, this is a lovely example of B&W, and the water power is tremendous - very well done, a deserved ribbon!! Comparing with the colour, the dress is so much better, more visible, a completely different mood, and the only possible thing which in my view could perhaps make a difference, would be to lighten the hair some, so that we could see a bit more texture. My apologies if you can, but my CRT monitor can''t show me any. The water looks so powerful, as it has texture - I think a longer exposure would show it more as smoke, which would destroy the power - most effective just as is.  I must admit that if I were going for a shot of the scene with no figure, I would love the colour shot, as they are lovely subtle colours - I don''t seem to be able to capture such myself, though I live just on the coast - sigh! Well done - will keep an eye for your future pix', '2008-10-15 06:57:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5009205, 728615, 30807, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot, Aimee - very good indeed! what a beautiful daughter shot too - I would probably have put it in as well, and then see who is fairest of them all - close tie?<br/> <br/>Anyway - I have this picture of you tottering on a stood in your studio, with your flexible big toe fishing around for the mid-air button, and the image is a hoot - (made me laugh, anyway), and I would have loved to see some of you trying to get the shot. Never mind, this is the real pix. I am most impressed with the shot in the mirror - your printer must be fantastic - which one is it?<br/> <br/>Anyway, congratulations on your ribbon - very well deserved!!!</td>', 'Lovely shot, Aimee - very good indeed! what a beautiful daughter shot too - I would probably have put it in as well, and then see who is fairest of them all - close tie? Anyway - I have this picture of you tottering on a stood in your studio, with your flexible big toe fishing around for the mid-air button, and the image is a hoot - (made me laugh, anyway), and I would have loved to see some of you trying to get the shot. Never mind, this is the real pix. I am most impressed with the shot in the mirror - your printer must be fantastic - which one is it? Anyway, congratulations on your ribbon - very well deserved!!!', '2008-10-15 07:11:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5009238, 727495, 23478, '<td valign="top">excellent image and the B&amp;W is just superb for this type of shot.  congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'excellent image and the B&W is just superb for this type of shot.  congrats on the ribbon.', '2008-10-15 07:48:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5009532, 728710, 52880, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous picture!!</td>', 'Gorgeous picture!!', '2008-10-15 11:34:33.000000', NULL, 0),
