(5010049, 727703, 31727, '<td valign="top">Butifully lighting.Great photograph.Very Vermir looking photograph.Did you use any fill light?grate photograph and very nicely lite.  Harvey Sherman</td>', 'Butifully lighting.Great photograph.Very Vermir looking photograph.Did you use any fill light?grate photograph and very nicely lite.  Harvey Sherman', '2008-10-15 15:29:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5010448, 728732, 61651, '<td valign="top">Now I get the "neighbor" reference from your comment on my shot - duh, I can be so thick.  The processing provides an appropriately maniacal feel to it, good for Rumpelstiltskin''s edginess, and I like how you got the back foliage to look fire-like, which also suits the story.</td>', 'Now I get the "neighbor" reference from your comment on my shot - duh, I can be so thick.  The processing provides an appropriately maniacal feel to it, good for Rumpelstiltskin''s edginess, and I like how you got the back foliage to look fire-like, which also suits the story.', '2008-10-15 18:39:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5010664, 728073, 73436, '<td valign="top">Excellent</td>', 'Excellent', '2008-10-15 20:55:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5010667, 727771, 68947, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your PB and Top Ten Finish!!!  Way to go!!!</td>', 'Congratulations on your PB and Top Ten Finish!!!  Way to go!!!', '2008-10-15 20:57:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5011061, 728655, 28742, '<td valign="top">Ha - I looked at this 3 times and hadn''t noticed the wolf til now.</td>', 'Ha - I looked at this 3 times and hadn''t noticed the wolf til now.', '2008-10-16 04:26:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5011430, 728709, 10686, '<td valign="top"><b>Hello from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>To start, it seems you have the technicals right on in this shot, exposure and color seem pretty well done.<br/> <br/>The connection to the story of Faithful John is tenuous at best, I''m pretty sure that the King''s faithful servant was not a football player.<br/> <br/>Compositionally, this is a bit of a mess. I can see how you attempted to shoot from a low angle and isolate the statue against the sky, but it''s not really very successful since the banner and the building (stadium?) remain quite prominent in the BG, which is distracting. You could have tried shooting with a wider aperture, but I''m not sure that would really help and would certainly blur the clouds/sky. <br/> <br/>The low angle also means that we''re left looking up at the subject, which, if not so extreme, can make someone appear taller and more in a position of authority. When taken to the extreme like this, we''re not really looking at their face, but more looking up their nose, which isn''t the most pleasant view.<br/> <br/>I''m not really sure what I can tell you how to improve this shot, but you should definitely keep shooting and consider everything in the frame, not just the subject.<br/> <br/>Cheers.</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club  To start, it seems you have the technicals right on in this shot, exposure and color seem pretty well done. The connection to the story of Faithful John is tenuous at best, I''m pretty sure that the King''s faithful servant was not a football player. Compositionally, this is a bit of a mess. I can see how you attempted to shoot from a low angle and isolate the statue against the sky, but it''s not really very successful since the banner and the building (stadium?) remain quite prominent in the BG, which is distracting. You could have tried shooting with a wider aperture, but I''m not sure that would really help and would certainly blur the clouds/sky.  The low angle also means that we''re left looking up at the subject, which, if not so extreme, can make someone appear taller and more in a position of authority. When taken to the extreme like this, we''re not really looking at their face, but more looking up their nose, which isn''t the most pleasant view. I''m not really sure what I can tell you how to improve this shot, but you should definitely keep shooting and consider everything in the frame, not just the subject. Cheers.', '2008-10-16 13:27:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5011467, 728516, 56275, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club! <br/> <br/>This is a technically beautiful shot. The lighting is spectacular. I especially like how the first set of stair rails pop. The composition and crop is great. Although, leaving in the corner of the front post may have been nice. Not a deal breaker though. <br/> <br/>The photo definitely sets the scene for a fairly tale, however, like many of the commenters, I feel it''s missing a subject. I realize this may have been hard to accomplish, as it seems you happened to be visiting there, and not necessarily going there with the intention to shoot for this challenge. Maybe someone would let you borrow their high heeled shoe. =)<br/> <br/>Overall, I think it''s a beautiful shot, and had the potential of being something amazing, if you had added a subject. I''m fairly certain that''s the only reason you were voted down.</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club!  This is a technically beautiful shot. The lighting is spectacular. I especially like how the first set of stair rails pop. The composition and crop is great. Although, leaving in the corner of the front post may have been nice. Not a deal breaker though.  The photo definitely sets the scene for a fairly tale, however, like many of the commenters, I feel it''s missing a subject. I realize this may have been hard to accomplish, as it seems you happened to be visiting there, and not necessarily going there with the intention to shoot for this challenge. Maybe someone would let you borrow their high heeled shoe. =) Overall, I think it''s a beautiful shot, and had the potential of being something amazing, if you had added a subject. I''m fairly certain that''s the only reason you were voted down.', '2008-10-16 14:13:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5011478, 728434, 56275, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club! <br/> <br/>I''m surprised by the low vote on this one. I think it''s a great macro shot, and I can see how it fits the challenge. However, I can also see how voters may not find it to fit the challenge as well as some other entries. <br/> <br/>Some suggestions for improvement.. A lot of the entries in this challenge had a lot to look at. The frames were very interesting, and I think they held the viewer''s attention. Your shot was well executed, and captured a bee in its natural environment, but after a few moments, there''s not much left to look at. I agree with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=76430" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">boyd2000</a> that expanding the DOF may have helped. I would have liked to see the detail of the far wing. But even with that, the background is not very interesting. <br/> <br/>If this were a macro challenge, I would have expected your score to be much higher. However with a challenge like Brother''s Grimm, I think the viewer goes into voting with the expectation of fairy tales, wonder, color and intrigue. Interesting that the top 13 shots focused on a human subject. <br/> <br/>It''s a good shot. Don''t get discouraged. I''m sure you know voter perception is hit or miss. You have an awesome portfolio. Looks like you re-tried your bee shot for the Work challenge, and you got top 10! Nice job.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  I''m surprised by the low vote on this one. I think it''s a great macro shot, and I can see how it fits the challenge. However, I can also see how voters may not find it to fit the challenge as well as some other entries.  Some suggestions for improvement.. A lot of the entries in this challenge had a lot to look at. The frames were very interesting, and I think they held the viewer''s attention. Your shot was well executed, and captured a bee in its natural environment, but after a few moments, there''s not much left to look at. I agree with  boyd2000 that expanding the DOF may have helped. I would have liked to see the detail of the far wing. But even with that, the background is not very interesting.  If this were a macro challenge, I would have expected your score to be much higher. However with a challenge like Brother''s Grimm, I think the viewer goes into voting with the expectation of fairy tales, wonder, color and intrigue. Interesting that the top 13 shots focused on a human subject.  It''s a good shot. Don''t get discouraged. I''m sure you know voter perception is hit or miss. You have an awesome portfolio. Looks like you re-tried your bee shot for the Work challenge, and you got top 10! Nice job.', '2008-10-16 14:31:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5011503, 728661, 56275, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Well, my first reaction was probably along the same lines as many of the voters. It''s messy, abstract, doesn''t seem to have a good focal point, and may be a stretch for the challenge. I think the title plays a very significant role in this shot. Without it, I don''t think anyone could guess what the shot is. However, with the title, it is very creative, and a different take compared to the many Red Riding Hood entries. It is a clever idea, and I like that you experimented with the CD holder and editing to get a unique feel. I just don''t think it compares to the clean, crisp, quality shots that DPC voters tend to adore. <br/> <br/>As for the shot itself, I can tell it''s taken in some sort of outdoor area, which fits the Riding Hood story, but the person doesn''t look much like a little girl in a red cape. She appears to be wearing jeans, hiking boots, and some sort of backpack? Little details like that may have improved the score. Maybe a picnic basket too. I''d also bring down the spiral blur a little, if possible.<br/> <br/>Your portfolio is filled with a wide range of shots. It appears you know how to appeal to voters, but also have a very creative, out of the box side of you. I applaud you for continuing to take these unique, interesting shots. It forces voters to look at shots they would otherwise pay not attention to. Keep it up!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Well, my first reaction was probably along the same lines as many of the voters. It''s messy, abstract, doesn''t seem to have a good focal point, and may be a stretch for the challenge. I think the title plays a very significant role in this shot. Without it, I don''t think anyone could guess what the shot is. However, with the title, it is very creative, and a different take compared to the many Red Riding Hood entries. It is a clever idea, and I like that you experimented with the CD holder and editing to get a unique feel. I just don''t think it compares to the clean, crisp, quality shots that DPC voters tend to adore.  As for the shot itself, I can tell it''s taken in some sort of outdoor area, which fits the Riding Hood story, but the person doesn''t look much like a little girl in a red cape. She appears to be wearing jeans, hiking boots, and some sort of backpack? Little details like that may have improved the score. Maybe a picnic basket too. I''d also bring down the spiral blur a little, if possible. Your portfolio is filled with a wide range of shots. It appears you know how to appeal to voters, but also have a very creative, out of the box side of you. I applaud you for continuing to take these unique, interesting shots. It forces voters to look at shots they would otherwise pay not attention to. Keep it up!', '2008-10-16 14:53:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(5011567, 728560, 10686, '<td valign="top"><b>From the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Technically, this is very well done from the exposure through the processing and the lighting is spot-on. Very well done.<br/> <br/>Your model may be a bit young to "be" Rapunzel, but I''d say she''s perfect as a little girl playing out the role in "pretend". The biggest issue is her expression. "Rapunzel" doesn''t look too happy to be rescued. I know from experience that getting 4 year olds to pose is a challenge, but, unfortunately, this one doesn''t quite make it.<br/> <br/>The only other thing I can think of is that the background is a nice combination of spring-like colors, but Rapunzel was imprisoned in a tall castle tower. It''s really a minor, but noticeable disconnect. <br/> <br/></td>', 'From the Critique Club  Technically, this is very well done from the exposure through the processing and the lighting is spot-on. Very well done. Your model may be a bit young to "be" Rapunzel, but I''d say she''s perfect as a little girl playing out the role in "pretend". The biggest issue is her expression. "Rapunzel" doesn''t look too happy to be rescued. I know from experience that getting 4 year olds to pose is a challenge, but, unfortunately, this one doesn''t quite make it. The only other thing I can think of is that the background is a nice combination of spring-like colors, but Rapunzel was imprisoned in a tall castle tower. It''s really a minor, but noticeable disconnect.  ', '2008-10-16 16:01:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5011811, 727495, 51269, '<td valign="top">I just realized this was yours....many congrats on this stunning image- Abigail is a wonderful girl - U must be so proud  :)</td>', 'I just realized this was yours....many congrats on this stunning image- Abigail is a wonderful girl - U must be so proud  :)', '2008-10-16 19:55:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5012010, 727771, 69668, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your top 10.  I love this tree!!!!  A very nice image indeed.</td>', 'Congrats on your top 10.  I love this tree!!!!  A very nice image indeed.', '2008-10-16 23:34:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5012081, 728698, 54728, '<td valign="top">I''ve been looking through and am honestly really liking this photo, though it did not score super well.  I really like the lighting and the quality of the image. It''s clear and a strong picture.  I like the slightly textured wall of the building.</td>', 'I''ve been looking through and am honestly really liking this photo, though it did not score super well.  I really like the lighting and the quality of the image. It''s clear and a strong picture.  I like the slightly textured wall of the building.', '2008-10-17 01:00:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5012083, 728674, 54728, '<td valign="top">Good job on thinking outside of the box!  I like it!</td>', 'Good job on thinking outside of the box!  I like it!', '2008-10-17 01:02:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5012270, 727495, 39830, '<td valign="top">Well done Ben!!! I knew I''d be seeing your name on the front page soon... it was just a matter of time. Please pass along a huge congrats to Abigail as well.</td>', 'Well done Ben!!! I knew I''d be seeing your name on the front page soon... it was just a matter of time. Please pass along a huge congrats to Abigail as well.', '2008-10-17 09:34:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5012413, 728615, 51269, '<td valign="top">Congrats on this amazing image---well deserved ribbon !!!</td>', 'Congrats on this amazing image---well deserved ribbon !!!', '2008-10-17 13:28:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5012503, 728708, 10686, '<td valign="top"><b>From the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>I think for the most part you were on the right track with the concept, it''s just lacking visually. <br/> <br/>Overall, my first impression is that this image certainly fits the challenge and the exposure looks OK, but the image is pretty mundane. There''s simply nothing drawing me in, no drama compelling me to keep looking. As others have commented, there are some styling issues with the blood looking like jelly or ketchup and the seam on the pillowcase. <br/> <br/>Let''s face it, there are only 3 things in this shot and they''re just sort of plopped in front of us, trying to tell a story or at least remind us of a story. I think it would have been much better to have a child or a weeping mother in the shot holding the rose. Barring that, the lighting could have been used to create some drama, the light you used here is pretty flat and really makes the scene dull.<br/> <br/>Cheers and keep shooting!<br/> <br/></td>', 'From the Critique Club  I think for the most part you were on the right track with the concept, it''s just lacking visually.  Overall, my first impression is that this image certainly fits the challenge and the exposure looks OK, but the image is pretty mundane. There''s simply nothing drawing me in, no drama compelling me to keep looking. As others have commented, there are some styling issues with the blood looking like jelly or ketchup and the seam on the pillowcase.  Let''s face it, there are only 3 things in this shot and they''re just sort of plopped in front of us, trying to tell a story or at least remind us of a story. I think it would have been much better to have a child or a weeping mother in the shot holding the rose. Barring that, the lighting could have been used to create some drama, the light you used here is pretty flat and really makes the scene dull. Cheers and keep shooting! ', '2008-10-17 15:13:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5012642, 728273, 67697, '<td valign="top">Glad to see you got some comments appreciating your photo.  I already sent you my thoughts.  She really does make a beautiful red riding hood!</td>', 'Glad to see you got some comments appreciating your photo.  I already sent you my thoughts.  She really does make a beautiful red riding hood!', '2008-10-17 17:07:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5012949, 728739, 62318, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot even though it may not fit the challenge directly it is still a wonderful capture.</td>', 'Beautiful shot even though it may not fit the challenge directly it is still a wonderful capture.', '2008-10-17 22:11:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5012981, 727703, 31727, '<td valign="top">I have commented on this photo/Its great thats what is very good.Did you plan to do this photo?And how did you it?It really grate.Did you use the key light from the sun?Or did you use strobes?  Harvey Sherman mrhsherman@yahoo.com.</td>', 'I have commented on this photo/Its great thats what is very good.Did you plan to do this photo?And how did you it?It really grate.Did you use the key light from the sun?Or did you use strobes?  Harvey Sherman mrhsherman@yahoo.com.', '2008-10-17 22:47:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5013051, 728123, 10686, '<td valign="top"><b>From the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Wow, this is really something cool. I''m not sure what I can offer other than to continue the accolades you''ve already gotten. Exposure-wise, you nailed it. Lighting the tree from below, combined with the low angle of view, really makes the tree stand out in a kind of creepy, haunted forest kind of way, especially with the strong orange sky. You''ve really done a great job with the "spirit" too. <br/> <br/>The only thing I can suggest that might have improved on this are to make the bottle a bit more obvious and maybe some costuming of the subject. These are really pretty minor.  And congratulations on a top ten finish.</td>', 'From the Critique Club  Wow, this is really something cool. I''m not sure what I can offer other than to continue the accolades you''ve already gotten. Exposure-wise, you nailed it. Lighting the tree from below, combined with the low angle of view, really makes the tree stand out in a kind of creepy, haunted forest kind of way, especially with the strong orange sky. You''ve really done a great job with the "spirit" too.  The only thing I can suggest that might have improved on this are to make the bottle a bit more obvious and maybe some costuming of the subject. These are really pretty minor.  And congratulations on a top ten finish.', '2008-10-18 00:43:35.000000', NULL, 0),
