(5023375, 728712, 62318, '<td valign="top">You are doing marvelous for your first four challenges! Keep it up. This is a fun take. I almost like the vibrant colors of the alternative, but still this was a strong showing. Good job.</td>', 'You are doing marvelous for your first four challenges! Keep it up. This is a fun take. I almost like the vibrant colors of the alternative, but still this was a strong showing. Good job.', '2008-10-24 13:16:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5023759, 728734, 68947, '<td valign="top">Ya know...this was excellently photographed!  It made me laugh.  I think that the Grimm''s challenge was a low scoring challenge to begin with.  This certainly didn''t deserve The Brown....but, hey......a ribbon is a ribbon!  Take it with pride!</td>', 'Ya know...this was excellently photographed!  It made me laugh.  I think that the Grimm''s challenge was a low scoring challenge to begin with.  This certainly didn''t deserve The Brown....but, hey......a ribbon is a ribbon!  Take it with pride!', '2008-10-24 18:00:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5023766, 728734, 68947, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by violinist123:</b></div><hr/><i> This isn''t really a shoehorn, the subject of the photo is an obvious attempt to meet the challenge via little red cap/little red riding hood imagery.  As one of your fifteen two votes, I can assure you that meeting the challenge is all that kept it from getting a 1 based purely on technical quality lol.  Gag shots score well sometimes if they are well shot.  I have proof. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I guess you just don''t like "shoehorns" because I''ve seen other shots do so much better and have NO focus!  Dancing Chicken Legs (Ballroom Blitz) was one....way back...gotta go look up that challenge again.  It wasn''t a shoehorn and it was not well shot.  Yet, it did much better.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-02-13 17:49:50.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by violinist123: This isn''t really a shoehorn, the subject of the photo is an obvious attempt to meet the challenge via little red cap/little red riding hood imagery.  As one of your fifteen two votes, I can assure you that meeting the challenge is all that kept it from getting a 1 based purely on technical quality lol.  Gag shots score well sometimes if they are well shot.  I have proof.   I guess you just don''t like "shoehorns" because I''ve seen other shots do so much better and have NO focus!  Dancing Chicken Legs (Ballroom Blitz) was one....way back...gotta go look up that challenge again.  It wasn''t a shoehorn and it was not well shot.  Yet, it did much better.', '2008-10-24 18:03:06.000000', '2009-02-13 17:49:50.000000', 0),
